  "body": "What: Add to the machine file a list of drill spindles: id, XY offset from the head origin, axis group (X row or Y row), tool number and fixed speed. Add a post template hook \"select spindle set\" so a drill operation can engage one or more spindles. The selection word is machine specific: public examples are an M-code per axis group, one tool number for each spindle, or one work offset `G54 Pxx` for each spindle.\n\nWhy: Drill blocks and gang drills are common on cabinet routers. No public standard exists, so each controller needs its own public source. First step: choose one controller with a public manual.\n\nSources: https://forums.autodesk.com/t5/hsm-post-processor-forum/syntec-with-drill-block/td-p/10710447 , https://mecsoft.com/blog/rhinocams-programmable-post-processor/ , https://www.homag.com/en/news-events/news/article/advanced-solutions-for-cnc-processing-and-drilling-technology-from-single-operation-to-interlinking-in-cells\n\nPart of #2395. Machine data for routers: see #1907 and #1918. Do not copy a vendor post (Clean-Room Protocol).\n\nDone means: a decision file names the first controller and its public source, a machine file with a drill block loads, and a golden G-code test shows the selection words for one and for several spindles.\n",
